# "Whenever one or more creatures an opponent controls attack you and aren't blocked": two unblocked Llanowar Elves are one event
# (CR 509.1h), so Bot2 draws three cards once, not six, gains control of the Jewel and untaps it (turn 4). It works both ways: on turn 5
# Bot1's Ornithopter attacks Bot2, who has no untapped blocker (the Elves are tapped from attacking), and Bot1 draws three and takes the
# Jewel back (CR 108.4).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Coveted Jewel
Ornithopter
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Llanowar Elves
Forest x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Coveted Jewel.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves; Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Coveted Jewel.Tapped = false
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 8
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Coveted Jewel.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot1.Hand.Count = 9
